    "text": "By Emily Burris Mia Villanueva ,\n5 hours ago PORTLAND, Ore. (KOIN) – For many people, obesity is often blamed on diet or lifestyle. For some, the cause is actually far more complex. Doctors say hypothalamic obesity, or HO, is a rare disease caused by injury or trauma to the brain, resulting in controllable hunger and rapid weight gain. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 1",
